{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.SelectionBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SelectionBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Exp","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SelectionBound.selection_needs_small_Np","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SelectionBound.selection_needs_small_Np","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SelectionBound.lean#L64-L74","doc":"The contrapositive, in the form a reviewer wants: to make a best-of-`N`\nresult surprising at level `α` — i.e. to force the chance of getting it by\nselection below `α` — the per-candidate probability must satisfy\n`N · p ≤ -log α`. With `N = 81` and `α = 0.05` that is `p ≤ 0.037`: each\nindividual candidate must already have been a 3.7 % shot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SelectionBound.menu_min_prob_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SelectionBound.menu_min_prob_ge","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SelectionBound.lean#L56-L62","doc":"**A menu minimum is expected, not surprising.** With `N` independent\ncandidates each landing inside the tolerance with probability `p`, the chance\nthat the best of them does is at least `1 - exp(-N p)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SelectionBound.pow_one_sub_le_exp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SelectionBound.pow_one_sub_le_exp","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SelectionBound.lean#L41-L54","doc":"`(1 - p)^N ≤ exp(-(N·p))` for `p ≤ 1`. The elementary step behind the\nselection bound. No lower bound on `p` is needed — only `1 - p ≥ 0`, so that\nthe power is monotone, and `1 - p ≤ exp(-p)`, which holds for every real. ","signatureChunk":0}]}